(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["R2"] = {"n":2,"level":"A2","t":"Reading Longer Everyday Texts","lessons":[{"id":"2.1","t":"Main Idea and Best Title","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.1 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Choose the best title for a short text.</p>\n<p>2. Reject titles that are too narrow or too broad.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يختار الطالب أفضل عنوان لنص قصير.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يستبعد العناوين الضيقة جدًا أو الواسعة جدًا.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A good title is like a label on a box: it tells you what is inside the WHOLE text. STEP often asks: Which is the best title for the text?</p>\n<p>Wrong titles usually fall into three groups: too narrow (only one detail), too broad (a much bigger topic than the text), or off-topic (words from the text but a different idea).</p>\n<p>The main idea is usually in the first or last sentence, and the other sentences support it with examples, reasons or details.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ Which is the best title for the text?</p>\n<p>▸ What is the text mainly about?</p>\n<p>▸ The main idea of the text is that …</p>\n<p>▸ Which title is too narrow for this text?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العنوان الجيد يشبه الملصق على الصندوق؛ يخبرك بمحتوى النص كله. والعناوين الخاطئة إما ضيقة جدًا (تفصيلة واحدة)، أو واسعة جدًا (موضوع أكبر من النص)، أو بعيدة عن الفكرة رغم أنها تستخدم كلمات من النص.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the first and the last sentence carefully.</p>\n<p>2. Ask: What is the writer talking about in EVERY sentence?</p>\n<p>3. Test each title: Does it cover the beginning, the middle and the end?</p>\n<p>4. Cross out titles that cover only one detail (too narrow).</p>\n<p>5. Cross out titles that are much bigger than the text (too broad).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ الجملة الأولى والأخيرة، واسأل: عن ماذا يتحدث الكاتب في كل جملة؟ ثم اختبر كل عنوان: هل يغطي البداية والوسط والنهاية؟ واحذف العنوان الضيق والعنوان الواسع.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Too narrow: a title about one example only.</p>\n<p>✗ Too broad: a title about a whole subject (Food in the World) when the text is about one food.</p>\n<p>✗ Copied words: a title that uses many words from the text but changes the idea.</p>\n<p>✗ A detail from the last sentence that is not the main point.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: A Garden on the Roof</strong></p>\n<p><em>(80 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Many families in big cities do not have a garden, so some of them are building gardens on their roofs. They grow tomatoes, mint and peppers in large pots. A roof garden keeps the house cooler in summer because the plants block some of the sun. It also gives children a place to learn about plants. In Riyadh, one family grows enough vegetables on their roof to cook a salad every day. Roof gardens are becoming more popular every year.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which is the best title for the text?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Tomatoes in Large Pots B. Gardens on City Roofs</p>\n<p>C. Plants of the World D. A Family in Riyadh</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Every sentence talks about roof gardens in cities.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A and D are single details (too narrow); C is too broad.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. What is the main idea of the text?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Roof gardens are useful and popular.</p>\n<p>B. Summer in Riyadh is very hot.</p>\n<p>C. Children like salad.</p>\n<p>D. Pots are expensive.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The text gives reasons (cool house, learning) and says they are popular.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العنوان الصحيح يغطي النص كله؛ استبعد التفصيلة الواحدة والموضوع الأكبر من النص.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 A","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–6): Why dates are a healthy snack","(126 words)","Dates are one of the oldest foods in Arabia, and today doctors say they are also one of the healthiest snacks. A few dates give you quick energy because they contain natural sugar. They also have fibre, which helps your stomach, and minerals such as potassium, which is good for your heart.","Many students eat crisps or chocolate during the break. These snacks are tasty, but they have a lot of salt, fat or added sugar. Three or four dates are a better choice. You can eat them with a glass of milk or a handful of nuts to feel full for longer. Of course, dates are sweet, so you should not eat too many. Brushing your teeth after eating them is a good idea too."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["The History of Arabia","Dates: A Healthy Snack for Students","How to Brush Your Teeth","Crisps and Chocolate"],"k":1,"e":"[best title] The whole text explains why dates are a healthy snack.","h":"العنوان الشامل."},{"n":2,"s":"What is the main idea of the first paragraph?","o":["Dates are an old Arabian food.","Potassium is good for the heart.","Doctors like dates more than milk.","Dates are good for your health."],"k":3,"e":"[main idea] The paragraph lists health benefits.","h":"فوائد التمر الصحية."},{"n":3,"s":"Why do dates give you quick energy?","o":["They have a lot of salt.","They contain natural sugar.","They are eaten with milk.","They contain fat."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] because they contain natural sugar.","h":"السكر الطبيعي."},{"n":4,"s":"According to the text, fibre …","o":["makes dates sweet","is bad for your teeth","helps your stomach","is found in crisps"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] fibre, which helps your stomach.","h":"الألياف تساعد المعدة."},{"n":5,"s":"Why should students not eat too many dates?","o":["Dates are very salty.","Dates are expensive.","Dates are hard to find.","Dates are sweet."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] dates are sweet, so you should not eat too many.","h":"لأن التمر حلو."},{"n":6,"s":"The title 'Snacks Around the World' is wrong because it is …","o":["too narrow","too broad","about one detail","exactly right"],"k":1,"e":"[best title] The text is about dates, not all snacks in the world.","h":"واسع جدًا."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 7–12): The first day at a new sports club","(126 words)","Last month, Rakan joined the Al-Hilal Youth Swimming Club. On his first day, he felt nervous because he did not know anyone. The coach, Captain Fawaz, smiled and introduced him to the other boys. Then he showed Rakan the changing rooms, the lockers and the two pools: a small one for beginners and a large one for racing.","The training started with warm-up exercises. After that, the boys swam four lengths of the small pool. Rakan was slower than the others, but nobody laughed. A boy called Mishal said, \"Don't worry. I was slow on my first day too.\" At the end of the session, Rakan felt tired but happy. He went home and told his parents that he wanted to go back the next day."],"q":[{"n":7,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["The Two Pools at Al-Hilal","Rakan's First Day at the Swimming Club","How to Swim Fast","Captain Fawaz's Family"],"k":1,"e":"[best title] The text follows Rakan's first day from start to end.","h":"يوم راكان الأول."},{"n":8,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a boy who feels welcome at a new club","a swimming race that Rakan won","the rules of a sports club","a coach who is very strict"],"k":0,"e":"[main idea] Rakan starts nervous and ends happy because people are kind.","h":"الشعور بالترحيب."},{"n":9,"s":"Why did Rakan feel nervous?","o":["He could not swim.","The coach was angry.","The pool was too deep.","He did not know anyone."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] because he did not know anyone.","h":"لا يعرف أحدًا."},{"n":10,"s":"What did the boys do after the warm-up?","o":["They swam four lengths of the small pool.","They raced in the large pool.","They went to the lockers.","They went home."],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] After that, the boys swam four lengths of the small pool.","h":"سبحوا أربعة أطوال."},{"n":11,"s":"Why did Mishal speak to Rakan?","o":["to ask him to leave","to laugh at him","to show him the lockers","to make him feel better"],"k":3,"e":"[inference] Don't worry. I was slow too — he encouraged Rakan.","h":"ليشجعه."},{"n":12,"s":"How did Rakan feel at the end of the session?","o":["angry and sad","bored","tired but happy","nervous and afraid"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] Rakan felt tired but happy.","h":"متعب لكنه سعيد."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 13–18): Visitors in the old town of AlUla","(125 words)","AlUla, in the north-west of Saudi Arabia, has become one of the country's most popular places for visitors. Its old town has more than 900 mud-brick houses. People lived in them for hundreds of years, but the last families left in the 1980s. Today, guides take visitors through the narrow streets and explain how life was in the past.","Visitors can also enjoy cafés, small shops and art workshops in the old town. In the evenings, the streets are lit with soft lights, and there is often traditional music. Many tourists come in winter, when the weather is cool and pleasant. In summer, the temperature can reach 45°C, so fewer people visit. The old town shows how AlUla mixes history with modern tourism."],"q":[{"n":13,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["Mud-Brick Houses in the World","Summer Weather in AlUla","A Café in the North-West","AlUla's Old Town: Past and Present"],"k":3,"e":"[best title] The text covers the history of the old town and visitors today.","h":"الماضي والحاضر."},{"n":14,"s":"What is the main idea of the second paragraph?","o":["AlUla is very hot in summer.","The last families left in the 1980s.","There are many things for visitors to enjoy in the old town.","Traditional music is played every night."],"k":2,"e":"[main idea] cafés, shops, workshops, lights, music.","h":"ما يستمتع به الزوار."},{"n":15,"s":"How many houses are there in the old town?","o":["about 90","exactly 1,980","more than 900","fewer than 500"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] more than 900 mud-brick houses.","h":"أكثر من 900."},{"n":16,"s":"When did the last families leave the old town?","o":["in winter","in the 1980s","hundreds of years ago","last year"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] the last families left in the 1980s.","h":"في الثمانينيات."},{"n":17,"s":"Why do fewer people visit in summer?","o":["It is very hot.","The shops are closed.","The guides are on holiday.","There is no music."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] temperature can reach 45°C, so fewer people visit.","h":"الحرارة الشديدة."},{"n":18,"s":"The word pleasant is closest in meaning to …","o":["very hot","crowded","nice and comfortable","dangerous"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] cool and pleasant weather → nice.","h":"لطيف."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 19–24): A school that plants trees every year","(125 words)","Every year in March, the students of Al-Faisal Intermediate School plant trees around their town. The idea started ten years ago, when a science teacher, Mr. Nasser, noticed that the area around the school had very little shade. He asked each class to plant one tree. That first year, the students planted twenty trees.","Now the project is much bigger. The students plant more than two hundred trees every spring, and the town council gives them the young trees for free. The students choose trees that need little water, such as neem and sidr. After planting, each class waters its trees twice a week until the summer holiday. Mr. Nasser says the trees make the streets cooler and teach students to care for their environment."],"q":[{"n":19,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["Mr. Nasser's Science Lessons","A School That Plants Trees Every Year","Neem and Sidr Trees","The Summer Holiday"],"k":1,"e":"[best title] The text is about the yearly tree-planting project.","h":"مشروع الزراعة السنوي."},{"n":20,"s":"What is the main idea of the text?","o":["Trees need water twice a week.","The town council sells trees.","A small school project has grown and helps the town.","March is the best month for science."],"k":2,"e":"[main idea] From twenty trees to over two hundred, making streets cooler.","h":"مشروع صغير كبر."},{"n":21,"s":"Why did Mr. Nasser start the project?","o":["There was little shade around the school.","The council asked him to.","The students wanted a holiday.","He wanted to sell trees."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] he noticed the area had very little shade.","h":"قلة الظل."},{"n":22,"s":"How many trees did the students plant in the first year?","o":["ten","two hundred","twenty","one"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] That first year, the students planted twenty trees.","h":"عشرون شجرة."},{"n":23,"s":"Why do the students choose neem and sidr trees?","o":["They grow fruit.","They are very tall.","They are cheap to buy.","They need little water."],"k":3,"e":"[detail] trees that need little water, such as neem and sidr.","h":"تحتاج ماءً قليلًا."},{"n":24,"s":"The word environment is closest in meaning to …","o":["the natural world around us","a school building","a kind of tree","a town council"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] care for their environment → nature around them.","h":"البيئة."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 25–30): Learning to swim as an adult","(124 words)","Many adults cannot swim, and some of them feel embarrassed about it. Abdulmajeed, a 38-year-old engineer from Dammam, was one of them. When his children started swimming lessons, he decided it was time to learn too. He joined an evening class for adults at a local sports centre.","At first, he was afraid to put his face in the water. His teacher was patient and started with simple steps: breathing, floating and kicking while holding the side of the pool. After six weeks, Abdulmajeed could swim ten metres. After three months, he swam a full length of the big pool. \"It is never too late to learn,\" he says. Now he swims with his children every weekend, and they are very proud of him."],"q":[{"n":25,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["Learning to Swim as an Adult","Swimming Lessons for Children","An Engineer from Dammam","The Big Pool at the Sports Centre"],"k":0,"e":"[best title] The text is about an adult who learns to swim.","h":"التعلم في الكبر."},{"n":26,"s":"What is the main idea of the text?","o":["Children swim better than adults.","Adults can learn to swim with patience and practice.","Engineers are very busy.","Swimming pools are dangerous."],"k":1,"e":"[main idea] It is never too late to learn.","h":"لم يفت الأوان."},{"n":27,"s":"Why did Abdulmajeed decide to learn to swim?","o":["His doctor told him to.","His work needed it.","He moved to Dammam.","His children started swimming lessons."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] When his children started swimming lessons, he decided …","h":"بسبب أطفاله."},{"n":28,"s":"What was difficult for him at first?","o":["kicking his legs","finding the sports centre","putting his face in the water","paying for lessons"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] he was afraid to put his face in the water.","h":"وضع وجهه في الماء."},{"n":29,"s":"How far could he swim after six weeks?","o":["ten metres","one full length","fifty metres","three metres"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] After six weeks, Abdulmajeed could swim ten metres.","h":"عشرة أمتار."},{"n":30,"s":"The word patient is closest in meaning to …","o":["calm and willing to wait","strict and angry","fast and strong","tired and bored"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] started with simple steps → calm, did not hurry.","h":"صبور."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.2","t":"Details in Longer Texts","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.2 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Locate details across several paragraphs.</p>\n<p>2. Avoid options that copy text words but change the meaning.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب التفاصيل في نص من عدة فقرات.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يتجنب البدائل التي تنسخ كلمات النص لكنها تغيّر المعنى.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>In longer texts, the answer to a detail question may be in any paragraph. First decide WHICH paragraph talks about the topic of the question, then read that part closely.</p>\n<p>STEP also asks simple NOT questions: Which of the following is NOT mentioned? Three options are in the text; the correct answer is the one that is missing or false.</p>\n<p>Be careful with options that copy many words from the text. They often change one small thing: a number, a person, a time or a negative word.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ According to the text, …</p>\n<p>▸ Which of the following is NOT mentioned in the text?</p>\n<p>▸ Which of the following is TRUE according to paragraph 2?</p>\n<p>▸ How many / How long / Where …?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في النصوص الأطول قد تكون الإجابة في أي فقرة، فحدد أولًا الفقرة التي تتحدث عن موضوع السؤال ثم اقرأها بدقة. وفي أسئلة NOT تكون ثلاثة بدائل موجودة في النص والإجابة هي البديل غير المذكور أو الخاطئ.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Underline the key word in the question.</p>\n<p>2. Skim the first sentence of each paragraph to find the right paragraph.</p>\n<p>3. Read the sentence with the answer slowly.</p>\n<p>4. For NOT questions, tick each option you find in the text; the option without a tick is the answer.</p>\n<p>5. Check small words: numbers, names, not, only, all.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدد الكلمة المفتاحية، واقرأ الجملة الأولى من كل فقرة لتعرف مكان الإجابة، ثم اقرأ الجملة ببطء. وفي أسئلة NOT ضع علامة على كل بديل موجود في النص، والبديل الباقي هو الإجابة. انتبه للأرقام والأسماء وكلمات النفي.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ The option copies text words but changes a number or a name.</p>\n<p>✗ The information is in the text but belongs to a different person or place.</p>\n<p>✗ In NOT questions, students choose the first option they find in the text.</p>\n<p>✗ The option is true in real life but not stated in the text.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: Our School Clinic</strong></p>\n<p><em>(60 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our school clinic is open from 7:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. The nurse, Mrs. Laila, helps students who feel ill or get small injuries.</p>\n<p>She keeps plasters, ice packs and a thermometer in the clinic. If a student has a high temperature, she calls the parents. She also gives short talks about healthy food every month.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which of the following is NOT mentioned as something in the clinic?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. plasters B. ice packs</p>\n<p>C. medicine for headaches D. a thermometer</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Tick what you find: plasters ✓, ice packs ✓, thermometer ✓.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Medicine for headaches is not mentioned.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. What does Mrs. Laila do if a student has a high temperature?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. She gives a talk. B. She calls the parents.</p>\n<p>C. She sends the student to class. D. She closes the clinic.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Key words: high temperature → paragraph 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> If a student has a high temperature, she calls the parents.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في سؤال NOT ضع علامة على كل ما تجده في النص، والبديل غير الموجود هو الإجابة.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 C · Example 2 B","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–6): A trip to the National Museum in Riyadh","(138 words)","Last week, our class visited the National Museum in Riyadh. We arrived at nine o'clock, and a guide called Mr. Salem met us at the entrance. He told us the museum has eight main halls, and that it opened in 1999.","First, we visited the hall about the creation of the universe. It had a large model of the planets and real pieces of meteorite. Then we went to the hall about Arabian kingdoms, where we saw old writing on stones and copies of ancient jewellery. My favourite hall was the one about the Prophet's mission, because it had beautiful maps and models of old Makkah and Madinah.","We had lunch in the museum café at twelve and then bought postcards in the gift shop. Our teacher asked us to write a report about one hall for homework."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"How many main halls does the museum have?","o":["nine","twelve","eight","nineteen"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] the museum has eight main halls.","h":"ثماني قاعات."},{"n":2,"s":"When did the museum open?","o":["last week","in 1999","at nine o'clock","in 2009"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] it opened in 1999.","h":"عام 1999."},{"n":3,"s":"What did the students see in the first hall?","o":["old writing on stones","maps of old Makkah","copies of ancient jewellery","a model of the planets and pieces of meteorite"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] First … a large model of the planets and real pieces of meteorite.","h":"نموذج الكواكب."},{"n":4,"s":"Why was the hall about the Prophet's mission the writer's favourite?","o":["It had beautiful maps and models.","It was the biggest hall.","It had a café inside.","The guide was there."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] because it had beautiful maps and models.","h":"الخرائط والنماذج."},{"n":5,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned in the text?","o":["a gift shop","a café","old writing on stones","a film about the desert"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] café ✓, gift shop ✓, writing on stones ✓; no film.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":6,"s":"What must the students do for homework?","o":["draw a map of Makkah","write a report about one hall","buy a postcard","visit the museum again"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] write a report about one hall for homework.","h":"كتابة تقرير."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 7–12): The life of a fisherman in Jazan","(133 words)","Uncle Hadi is a fisherman in Jazan, on the Red Sea coast. He has fished for more than thirty years, like his father and grandfather before him. He leaves home at four in the morning, before the sun rises, and sails his small wooden boat about ten kilometres from the coast.","He uses nets to catch fish such as hamour, kingfish and parrotfish. On a good day, he catches about forty kilograms, but in bad weather he may catch nothing. Strong winds in summer sometimes stop him from going out for several days.","By ten o'clock he returns to the port and sells his fish at the market. Restaurants buy the best fish first. Uncle Hadi says the work is hard, but he loves the sea and the quiet of the early morning."],"q":[{"n":7,"s":"How long has Uncle Hadi been a fisherman?","o":["more than thirty years","about ten years","forty years exactly","since last summer"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] He has fished for more than thirty years.","h":"أكثر من ثلاثين سنة."},{"n":8,"s":"What time does he leave home?","o":["at ten in the morning","after sunrise","at four in the morning","at midnight"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] He leaves home at four in the morning.","h":"الرابعة فجرًا."},{"n":9,"s":"How far from the coast does he usually go?","o":["about ten kilometres","about forty kilometres","about four kilometres","about thirty kilometres"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] about ten kilometres from the coast.","h":"عشرة كيلومترات."},{"n":10,"s":"Which fish is NOT mentioned in the text?","o":["hamour","tuna","kingfish","parrotfish"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] hamour ✓ kingfish ✓ parrotfish ✓; tuna ✗.","h":"التونة غير مذكورة."},{"n":11,"s":"What sometimes stops him from fishing in summer?","o":["strong winds","high prices","a broken net","the restaurants"],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] Strong winds in summer sometimes stop him.","h":"الرياح القوية."},{"n":12,"s":"Who buys the best fish first?","o":["restaurants","his neighbours","other fishermen","tourists"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Restaurants buy the best fish first.","h":"المطاعم."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 13–18): A school science fair","(135 words)","On Tuesday, our school held its yearly science fair in the sports hall. Forty students from Grades 7 to 9 showed their projects to parents, teachers and three judges from the local university.","The projects were very different. Faris made a small car that runs on solar power. Two girls from Grade 8 tested which drinks damage teeth the most by putting eggshells in cola, juice and milk for a week. Another student built a simple weather station that measured wind speed and rainfall.","The judges gave first prize to Faris's solar car because it was cheap to build and worked well. The eggshell project came second. The winners received certificates and a visit to a science centre in Dhahran. The head teacher said next year's fair will be open to Grade 6 as well."],"q":[{"n":13,"s":"Where was the science fair held?","o":["at the university","in the library","in the sports hall","at a science centre"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] in the sports hall.","h":"صالة الرياضة."},{"n":14,"s":"Who were the judges?","o":["the parents of the students","teachers from Grade 9","students from Dhahran","three people from a local university"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] three judges from the local university.","h":"من الجامعة."},{"n":15,"s":"What did the two girls use in their project?","o":["solar panels","eggshells","a weather station","toy cars"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] putting eggshells in cola, juice and milk.","h":"قشر البيض."},{"n":16,"s":"Why did Faris's project win?","o":["It was cheap to build and worked well.","It was the biggest project.","It measured rainfall.","It was about teeth."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] because it was cheap to build and worked well.","h":"رخيص ويعمل جيدًا."},{"n":17,"s":"Which of the following is TRUE?","o":["Forty judges visited the fair.","Grade 6 students showed projects this year.","The eggshell project won second prize.","The weather station won first prize."],"k":2,"e":"[detail] The eggshell project came second.","h":"الصحيح."},{"n":18,"s":"What prize did the winners get?","o":["money and books","certificates and a trip to a science centre","a solar car","a free year at university"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] certificates and a visit to a science centre in Dhahran.","h":"شهادات وزيارة."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 19–24): A family moves to a new apartment","(136 words)","Last month, the Al-Qahtani family moved from a small house in Abha to a new apartment in Khobar. Mr. Al-Qahtani got a new job at a company there, so the family had to move. It was a long journey of more than 1,200 kilometres.","The new apartment is on the fifth floor of a modern building. It has three bedrooms, two bathrooms and a balcony with a view of the sea. There is a lift, a small gym and a car park under the building. The children, Lama and Bassam, share a bedroom for now.","Mrs. Al-Qahtani misses the cool weather and green mountains of Abha. However, she likes being close to the sea and the big supermarkets. Bassam has already joined a football team, and Lama has made two friends at her new school."],"q":[{"n":19,"s":"Why did the family move to Khobar?","o":["The children wanted to live by the sea.","Their house in Abha was too big.","Mrs. Al-Qahtani was ill.","Mr. Al-Qahtani got a new job there."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] got a new job at a company there, so the family had to move.","h":"عمل جديد."},{"n":20,"s":"On which floor is the new apartment?","o":["the first","the fifth","the third","the twelfth"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] on the fifth floor.","h":"الطابق الخامس."},{"n":21,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned about the building?","o":["a lift","a small gym","a swimming pool","a car park"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] lift ✓ gym ✓ car park ✓; pool ✗.","h":"المسبح غير مذكور."},{"n":22,"s":"What does Mrs. Al-Qahtani miss about Abha?","o":["the big supermarkets","the cool weather and green mountains","her old job","the sea view"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] misses the cool weather and green mountains of Abha.","h":"الطقس والجبال."},{"n":23,"s":"Which of the following is TRUE?","o":["The apartment has four bedrooms.","Bassam has made two friends.","The journey was 200 kilometres.","Lama and Bassam share a bedroom."],"k":3,"e":"[detail] The children, Lama and Bassam, share a bedroom for now.","h":"الصحيح."},{"n":24,"s":"What has Bassam done since the move?","o":["joined a football team","made two friends","started a new job","visited Abha again"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Bassam has already joined a football team.","h":"انضم لفريق."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 25–30): The rules of a youth football league","(137 words)","The Al-Noor Youth Football League is open to boys aged 10 to 14. Each team has twelve players: seven on the field and five reserves. Matches are played on Saturday mornings from October to March.","Every player must wear the team shirt, shin pads and football boots. Players without shin pads cannot play, for their own safety. A match has two halves of twenty-five minutes, with a ten-minute break in the middle. Every player in the team must play for at least fifteen minutes in each match, so coaches cannot use only their best players.","Fair play is very important. A player who receives two yellow cards in one match must leave the field. At the end of the season, there is a prize for the top team and another for the team with the best behaviour."],"q":[{"n":25,"s":"Who can join the league?","o":["boys under 10","boys aged 10 to 14","anyone over 14","only team coaches"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] open to boys aged 10 to 14.","h":"من 10 إلى 14."},{"n":26,"s":"How many players does each team have?","o":["seven","five","fourteen","twelve"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Each team has twelve players.","h":"اثنا عشر."},{"n":27,"s":"How long is a full match, without the break?","o":["twenty-five minutes","sixty minutes","fifteen minutes","fifty minutes"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] two halves of twenty-five minutes = 50.","h":"خمسون دقيقة."},{"n":28,"s":"Why must every player play for at least fifteen minutes?","o":["because matches are very long","so that players can rest","so coaches do not use only their best players","because the field is small"],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] so coaches cannot use only their best players.","h":"ليشارك الجميع."},{"n":29,"s":"Which of the following is NOT a rule in the text?","o":["Players must wear shin pads.","Two yellow cards mean leaving the field.","Matches are on Saturday mornings.","Players must bring their own ball."],"k":3,"e":"[detail] No rule about bringing a ball.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":30,"s":"What are the two prizes at the end of the season?","o":["one for the best coach and one for the best player","one for the most goals and one for the best shirt","one for the top team and one for the best behaviour","one for October and one for March"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] a prize for the top team and another for the best behaviour.","h":"الجائزتان."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.3","t":"Vocabulary in Context: Synonyms and Antonyms","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.3 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use context to find synonyms and antonyms.</p>\n<p>2. Recognize contrast and definition clues (but, however, which means).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب السياق لإيجاد المرادف والضد.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يتعرف على قرائن التضاد والتعريف مثل but وhowever وwhich means.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>At A2, STEP asks two kinds of word questions: The word X is closest in meaning to … (a synonym) and The word X is the opposite of … (an antonym).</p>\n<p>Contrast clues (but, however, although, while) tell you that the next idea is the opposite. Definition clues (which means, that is, or, a dash —) explain the word directly.</p>\n<p>Example: The room was messy, but after an hour it was tidy. The word but shows that tidy is the opposite of messy.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The word … is closest in meaning to …</p>\n<p>▸ The word … is the opposite of …</p>\n<p>▸ Which word in paragraph 2 means …?</p>\n<p>▸ The underlined word could best be replaced by …</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يسأل اختبار STEP عن المرادف (closest in meaning) وعن الضد (the opposite of). وكلمات التضاد مثل but وhowever وalthough تدل على معنى معاكس، وكلمات التعريف مثل which means وthat is تشرح الكلمة مباشرة.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the word and read the whole sentence.</p>\n<p>2. Look for a clue word: but / however (opposite), and / also (similar), which means / that is (definition).</p>\n<p>3. Decide if the word is positive or negative.</p>\n<p>4. Put each option in place of the word and read the sentence.</p>\n<p>5. For antonym questions, check you are choosing the OPPOSITE, not the synonym.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ الجملة كاملة، وابحث عن كلمة القرينة: but للتضاد، وand للتشابه، وwhich means للتعريف. ثم حدد إن كانت الكلمة إيجابية أم سلبية، وضع كل بديل مكان الكلمة. وفي سؤال الضد تأكد أنك تختار العكس لا المرادف.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Choosing the synonym when the question asks for the opposite.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing a word that is related to the topic but not the same meaning.</p>\n<p>✗ Ignoring the contrast word but or however.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing the most common meaning instead of the meaning in the sentence.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: A Busy Market</strong></p>\n<p><em>(37 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In the morning, the vegetable market is crowded; hundreds of people push past each other to buy fresh food. However, by two o'clock it is almost deserted, and only a few sellers stay to clean their stalls.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The word crowded is closest in meaning to …</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. full of people B. very clean C. very cheap D. quiet</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Clue after the semicolon: hundreds of people push past each other.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> So crowded = full of people.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The word deserted is the opposite of …</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. cheap B. crowded C. fresh D. clean</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> However shows contrast with the morning.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Deserted = empty; its opposite is crowded.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">however تعني أن الفكرة التالية عكس السابقة؛ لذلك deserted (فارغ) عكس crowded (مزدحم).</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 A · Example 2 B","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–6): A hot afternoon and a cool evening in the desert","(123 words)","Last week, my family went camping in the desert near Riyadh. In the afternoon, the sun was scorching, and the sand was too hot to walk on without shoes. We stayed inside the tent and drank a lot of cold water. My little brother was miserable; he complained all afternoon.","However, the evening was completely different. After sunset, the air became cool and fresh, and a gentle wind blew across the dunes. We made a fire, cooked chicken and drank sweet tea. My brother forgot his bad mood and was cheerful again; he sang songs and laughed with my cousins. Later, the sky was so clear that we could see thousands of stars. We all agreed that the desert at night is magical."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"The word scorching is closest in meaning to …","o":["extremely hot","very windy","pleasant","cloudy"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] the sand was too hot to walk on → extremely hot.","h":"حارق."},{"n":2,"s":"The word miserable is the opposite of …","o":["cheerful","tired","cold","hungry"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] He forgot his bad mood and was cheerful again.","h":"عكس miserable."},{"n":3,"s":"The word gentle is closest in meaning to …","o":["strong and loud","soft and light","hot and dry","sudden"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] a gentle wind in a cool, fresh evening → soft.","h":"لطيف خفيف."},{"n":4,"s":"Which word in paragraph 2 shows that the evening was different from the afternoon?","o":["After","Later","so","However"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] However is a contrast word.","h":"كلمة التضاد."},{"n":5,"s":"Why did the family stay inside the tent in the afternoon?","o":["It was raining.","They were cooking.","It was too hot outside.","They were sleeping."],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] the sun was scorching … We stayed inside.","h":"الحر الشديد."},{"n":6,"s":"The word magical is closest in meaning to …","o":["frightening","wonderful and special","boring","dangerous"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] stars, cool air, songs → wonderful.","h":"ساحر."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 7–12): A messy room that became tidy","(132 words)","Ziyad's bedroom was always messy. His clothes were on the floor, his books were under the bed, and there were empty juice bottles on his desk. His mother often asked him to clean it, but he always said, \"Later.\"","One day, he could not find his football boots before an important match. He searched for half an hour and missed the team bus. That evening, he decided to change. He sorted his things into three boxes: keep, give away and throw away. He put his books on a shelf and hung his clothes in the wardrobe.","Now his room is neat and tidy. Ziyad says it takes only five minutes a day to keep it that way. He can find everything quickly, and he even has space to do push-ups before school."],"q":[{"n":7,"s":"The word messy is the opposite of …","o":["empty","important","tidy","quick"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Now his room is neat and tidy — the opposite of before.","h":"عكس messy."},{"n":8,"s":"The word sorted is closest in meaning to …","o":["threw away","put into groups","lost","washed"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] sorted his things into three boxes → grouped.","h":"صنّف."},{"n":9,"s":"The word neat is closest in meaning to …","o":["clean and in order","very small","full of boxes","dark"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] neat and tidy → in order.","h":"مرتب."},{"n":10,"s":"What made Ziyad decide to change?","o":["His mother threw away his books.","His friends visited his room.","He bought a new wardrobe.","He missed the team bus because he could not find his boots."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] could not find his boots … missed the team bus … decided to change.","h":"فاتته الحافلة."},{"n":11,"s":"Which of the following is NOT one of Ziyad's three boxes?","o":["keep","repair","give away","throw away"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] keep, give away and throw away.","h":"ليس من الصناديق."},{"n":12,"s":"How long does Ziyad spend each day keeping his room tidy?","o":["half an hour","one hour","five minutes","fifteen minutes"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] it takes only five minutes a day.","h":"خمس دقائق."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 13–18): A shy student who became confident","(135 words)","When Reem started Grade 7, she was very shy. She sat at the back of the class and never raised her hand, although she often knew the answers. When the teacher asked her a question, her face turned red and she spoke in a very quiet voice.","Her English teacher, Ms. Hind, noticed this. She invited Reem to join the school radio club, which prepares a short programme every morning. At first, Reem only wrote the news. Then Ms. Hind asked her to read one sentence on the radio. Her hands were shaking, but she did it.","Slowly, Reem became more confident. By the end of the year, she was presenting the whole programme in front of the microphone. Her parents were amazed. Now she answers questions in class and even helps other shy students."],"q":[{"n":13,"s":"The word shy is the opposite of …","o":["confident","quiet","red","tired"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] She was shy … slowly became more confident.","h":"عكس shy."},{"n":14,"s":"The word although in paragraph 1 shows …","o":["a surprising contrast","a reason","a time","an example"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] never raised her hand although she knew the answers → contrast.","h":"تضاد."},{"n":15,"s":"What did Reem do first in the radio club?","o":["She read one sentence.","She wrote the news.","She presented the programme.","She helped shy students."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence] At first, Reem only wrote the news.","h":"كتبت الأخبار."},{"n":16,"s":"The word shaking is closest in meaning to …","o":["holding something tightly","very clean","very cold and dry","moving quickly because of fear"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] She was nervous; her hands were shaking.","h":"ترتجف."},{"n":17,"s":"The word amazed is closest in meaning to …","o":["very angry","a little worried","very surprised","bored"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Her parents were amazed by the big change.","h":"مندهش."},{"n":18,"s":"Who helped Reem become confident?","o":["her parents","her English teacher","the head teacher","another shy student"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Her English teacher, Ms. Hind, noticed this and invited her.","h":"المعلمة."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 19–24): Old and new houses in Jeddah's Al-Balad","(137 words)","Jeddah's historic district, Al-Balad, is more than a thousand years old. Its traditional houses are tall and narrow, with four or five floors. They are made of coral stone from the Red Sea, and they have large wooden windows called rawashin. These windows let the sea breeze in and keep the rooms cool, so the houses do not need air conditioners.","Modern houses in Jeddah are very different. Most are made of concrete and glass, and many are wide rather than tall. They often have gardens and garages, but they need air conditioners for most of the year.","Some people think the old houses are inconvenient because they have many stairs and no lifts. However, others think they are beautiful and should be protected. Today, many old houses are being restored as hotels, cafés and museums."],"q":[{"n":19,"s":"The word narrow is the opposite of …","o":["tall","old","cool","wide"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Modern houses … are wide rather than tall; narrow ↔︎ wide.","h":"عكس narrow."},{"n":20,"s":"The word breeze is closest in meaning to …","o":["a big wave","strong sunlight","heavy rain","a light wind"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] sea breeze … keeps the rooms cool → light wind.","h":"نسيم."},{"n":21,"s":"What are rawashin?","o":["coral stones","small gardens","large wooden windows","air conditioners"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] large wooden windows called rawashin.","h":"رواشين = نوافذ خشبية."},{"n":22,"s":"The word inconvenient is closest in meaning to …","o":["not easy to use","very expensive","very beautiful","very modern"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] many stairs and no lifts → not easy.","h":"غير مريح / غير عملي."},{"n":23,"s":"The word restored is closest in meaning to …","o":["knocked down","sold cheaply","painted black","repaired and made good again"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] old houses being restored as hotels and cafés → repaired.","h":"تُرمّم."},{"n":24,"s":"Which of the following is TRUE about modern houses in the text?","o":["They need air conditioners for most of the year.","They are made of coral stone.","They have rawashin.","They are more than a thousand years old."],"k":0,"e":"[detail] they need air conditioners for most of the year.","h":"الصحيح."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 25–30): An easy recipe and a difficult one","(133 words)","Some recipes are simple, while others are complicated. A good example of a simple recipe is a fruit salad. You only need a knife, a bowl and some fresh fruit, such as apples, bananas and oranges. You chop the fruit, mix it and add a little honey. It takes about ten minutes, and even young children can make it.","Kabsa, on the other hand, is much more complicated. First, you must fry onions and chicken with many spices. Then you add tomatoes, water and rice, and you must watch the pot carefully so the rice does not burn. You also need to fry nuts and raisins for the top. The whole process can take nearly two hours.","Beginners should start with easy dishes and try difficult ones later, when they feel more experienced."],"q":[{"n":25,"s":"The word complicated is the opposite of …","o":["delicious","careful","simple","fresh"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Some recipes are simple, while others are complicated.","h":"عكس complicated."},{"n":26,"s":"The word while in sentence 1 shows …","o":["a reason","a result","an example","a contrast between two ideas"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] simple ↔︎ complicated → contrast.","h":"تضاد."},{"n":27,"s":"The phrase on the other hand introduces …","o":["a different, opposite example","the same idea again","a list of fruits","the end of the recipe"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Kabsa, on the other hand, is much more complicated.","h":"مثال معاكس."},{"n":28,"s":"The word chop is closest in meaning to …","o":["cook in oil","wash in water","buy at a shop","cut into pieces"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] You need a knife … chop the fruit → cut.","h":"يقطّع."},{"n":29,"s":"Why must you watch the pot carefully?","o":["so the chicken stays cold","so the rice does not burn","so the honey is sweet","so the nuts are fresh"],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] so the rice does not burn.","h":"حتى لا يحترق الأرز."},{"n":30,"s":"The word experienced is the opposite of …","o":["difficult","careful","beginner","later"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Beginners … later, when they feel more experienced.","h":"عكس experienced."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.4","t":"Sequence of Events","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.4 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Order events using time words (first, then, after that, finally).</p>\n<p>2. Answer what happened before / after questions.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يرتب الطالب الأحداث باستخدام كلمات الزمن مثل first وthen وafter that وfinally.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يجيب عن أسئلة ماذا حدث قبل / بعد.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Many texts describe a process (how something is made or done) or a story (what happened). STEP asks: What happened after …? What is the first / last step? Which comes between X and Y?</p>\n<p>Time and order words help you: first, next, then, after that, later, before, after, while, when, as soon as, finally, in the end.</p>\n<p>Be careful: the order in the sentence is not always the order in time. Before you leave, check the door means checking happens FIRST.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ What happens after …?</p>\n<p>▸ What is the first step in …?</p>\n<p>▸ Which of the following happens last?</p>\n<p>▸ What did … do before …?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تصف نصوص كثيرة عملية أو قصة، ويسأل الاختبار: ماذا حدث بعد…؟ ما الخطوة الأولى؟ ما الذي يأتي بين…؟ واستعن بكلمات الترتيب مثل first وthen وafter that وfinally. وانتبه: ترتيب الكلمات في الجملة ليس دائمًا ترتيب الأحداث في الزمن، ففي Before you leave, check the door يأتي التحقق أولًا.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Circle all the time and order words in the text.</p>\n<p>2. Number the events 1, 2, 3 in the margin as you read.</p>\n<p>3. For before / after questions, find the event named in the question first.</p>\n<p>4. Look one step backward (before) or one step forward (after).</p>\n<p>5. Check sentences with before, after and when: the event after before happens SECOND.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ضع دائرة حول كلمات الزمن والترتيب، ورقّم الأحداث في الهامش. وفي أسئلة before وafter حدد الحدث المذكور في السؤال، ثم انتقل خطوة للخلف أو للأمام. وتذكّر أن الحدث بعد before يقع ثانيًا.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Choosing the event that is mentioned next in the text, but happens earlier in time.</p>\n<p>✗ Confusing before and after.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing a step from a different part of the process.</p>\n<p>✗ Missing a step that has no order word.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: Making Mint Tea</strong></p>\n<p><em>(50 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>First, boil some water in a kettle. While the water is boiling, put two spoons of tea and a few fresh mint leaves in a teapot. When the water is ready, pour it into the teapot. Before you serve the tea, wait three minutes and add sugar if you like.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. What do you do while the water is boiling?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. pour the water into the teapot B. put tea and mint in the teapot</p>\n<p>C. add sugar D. serve the tea</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> While = at the same time.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> While the water is boiling, put two spoons of tea and mint.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. What is the last step?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. boil the water B. pour the water</p>\n<p>C. wait three minutes D. serve the tea</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Before you serve the tea, wait three minutes → serve comes after waiting.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Serving is last.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is D.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">while تعني في الوقت نفسه، وbefore you serve تعني أن التقديم يأتي بعد الانتظار.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 D","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–6): How a parcel reaches your home","(134 words)","When you order something online, it goes on a long journey before it reaches your door. First, the online shop receives your order and payment. Then a worker in a large warehouse finds the item on a shelf and puts it in a box with a label.","After that, the box goes on a lorry to a sorting centre. There, machines read the labels and send each parcel to the right city. Next, the parcel travels by lorry or plane to a local delivery office near your home.","Finally, a delivery driver collects the parcel in the morning and brings it to your address. Before the driver leaves, he takes a photo of the parcel at your door or asks you to sign for it. The whole process usually takes two to five days."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What is the first step in the process?","o":["A worker finds the item.","Machines read the labels.","A driver collects the parcel.","The shop receives the order and payment."],"k":3,"e":"[sequence] First, the online shop receives your order and payment.","h":"الخطوة الأولى."},{"n":2,"s":"What happens just after the worker puts the item in a box?","o":["The box goes on a lorry to a sorting centre.","The driver takes a photo.","The shop receives payment.","The parcel reaches your home."],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] After that, the box goes on a lorry to a sorting centre.","h":"بعدها مباشرة."},{"n":3,"s":"Where do machines read the labels?","o":["in the warehouse","at your home","in the shop","at the sorting centre"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] There (sorting centre), machines read the labels.","h":"مركز الفرز."},{"n":4,"s":"What does the driver do before he leaves?","o":["takes a photo or asks you to sign","finds the item on a shelf","drives to the sorting centre","receives your payment"],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] Before the driver leaves, he takes a photo … or asks you to sign.","h":"قبل المغادرة."},{"n":5,"s":"Which step comes between the sorting centre and the driver collecting the parcel?","o":["A worker puts a label on the box.","The shop receives the order.","The parcel travels to a local delivery office.","You sign for the parcel."],"k":2,"e":"[sequence] Next, the parcel travels … to a local delivery office.","h":"الخطوة الوسطى."},{"n":6,"s":"How long does the whole process usually take?","o":["one day","about a week","five hours","two to five days"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] usually takes two to five days.","h":"يومان إلى خمسة."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 7–12): Growing a tomato plant from a seed","(145 words)","Growing a tomato plant from a seed is easy and fun. To begin with, fill a small pot with soil and press one or two seeds about one centimetre into it. Water the soil gently and put the pot in a warm, sunny place.","After seven to ten days, a small green shoot will appear. Keep the soil wet, but not too wet. When the plant is about fifteen centimetres tall, move it into a bigger pot or into the garden. At this stage, push a stick into the soil next to it, because the plant will need support as it grows.","About six weeks later, yellow flowers will appear. Bees and wind help the flowers to make fruit. Small green tomatoes grow first, and they slowly turn red. Finally, when they are red and a little soft, you can pick them and eat them."],"q":[{"n":7,"s":"What is the first thing you do?","o":["water the soil","fill a small pot with soil","put the pot in the sun","press the seeds into the soil"],"k":1,"e":"[sequence] To begin with, fill a small pot with soil.","h":"الخطوة الأولى."},{"n":8,"s":"When does a small green shoot appear?","o":["after seven to ten days","after six weeks","after one day","after the flowers appear"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] After seven to ten days, a small green shoot will appear.","h":"بعد 7 إلى 10 أيام."},{"n":9,"s":"When should you move the plant into a bigger pot?","o":["when it is about fifteen centimetres tall","when the flowers appear","when the tomatoes are red","before the shoot appears"],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] When the plant is about fifteen centimetres tall, move it.","h":"عند طول 15 سم."},{"n":10,"s":"Why do you push a stick into the soil?","o":["The stick keeps the soil wet.","Bees like sticks.","The plant will need support.","It makes the tomatoes red."],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] because the plant will need support as it grows.","h":"للدعم."},{"n":11,"s":"What happens before the tomatoes turn red?","o":["You pick the tomatoes.","Small green tomatoes grow.","You plant the seeds again.","The flowers turn red."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence] Small green tomatoes grow first, and they slowly turn red.","h":"قبل الاحمرار."},{"n":12,"s":"The word shoot in paragraph 2 means …","o":["a hard kick with the foot","a photo","a small seed","a new young part of a plant"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] a small green shoot appears from the soil.","h":"برعم."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 13–18): A family evening at Riyadh Season","(126 words)","Last Thursday, my family spent the evening at Riyadh Season. We left home at six o'clock, and the roads were busy, so we arrived at Boulevard City at seven. As soon as we entered, my little sisters ran to the giant lanterns and took photos.","After that, we watched a show with dancing water and coloured lights. It lasted twenty minutes, and the music was amazing. Then my father bought us tickets for the big wheel. From the top, we could see the whole area shining in the dark.","Later, we were hungry, so we ate burgers at a restaurant near the lake. Before we went home, my mother bought small gifts for my grandparents. We got back home at midnight, very tired but very happy."],"q":[{"n":13,"s":"What did the sisters do as soon as they entered?","o":["They watched the water show.","They ran to the lanterns and took photos.","They rode the big wheel.","They ate burgers."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence] As soon as we entered, my little sisters ran to the giant lanterns.","h":"فور الدخول."},{"n":14,"s":"Why did the family arrive at seven?","o":["They left home late.","The car broke down.","They stopped to buy gifts.","The roads were busy."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] the roads were busy, so we arrived at seven.","h":"الزحام."},{"n":15,"s":"What did the family do right after the water show?","o":["They rode the big wheel.","They took photos of the lanterns.","They ate at a restaurant.","They went home."],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] Then my father bought us tickets for the big wheel.","h":"بعد العرض."},{"n":16,"s":"How long was the water show?","o":["one hour","ten minutes","twenty minutes","five hours"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] It lasted twenty minutes.","h":"عشرون دقيقة."},{"n":17,"s":"What did the mother do before they went home?","o":["took photos of the lanterns","bought tickets for the big wheel","bought small gifts for the grandparents","cooked dinner"],"k":2,"e":"[sequence] Before we went home, my mother bought small gifts.","h":"قبل العودة."},{"n":18,"s":"Which of these happened last?","o":["They ate burgers.","The family got back home.","They watched the water show.","They saw the area from the big wheel."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence] We got back home at midnight.","h":"الأخير."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 19–24): Getting ready for a school trip to Taif","(143 words)","Dear Parents,","Our Grade 8 trip to Taif will take place next Wednesday. Please read the plan carefully. One week before the trip, students must return the signed permission form to their class teacher. Two days before, they should pack a small bag with a jacket, a water bottle, sunscreen and a snack.","On the morning of the trip, students must arrive at school by 6:15 a.m. The teachers will check names before the students get on the bus. The bus will leave at 6:30 and arrive in Taif at about 9:00. First, we will visit Al-Shafa rose farms, and then we will have lunch at Al-Rudaf Park. After lunch, students will ride the cable car at Al-Hada.","We will return to school at about 7:00 p.m. Please collect your child on time.","Mr. Badr, Trip Organizer"],"q":[{"n":19,"s":"What must students do one week before the trip?","o":["return the signed permission form","pack a small bag","arrive at school at 6:15","ride the cable car"],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] One week before the trip, students must return the signed permission form.","h":"قبل أسبوع."},{"n":20,"s":"What happens before the students get on the bus?","o":["They visit the rose farms.","The teachers check names.","They have lunch.","They pack their bags."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence] The teachers will check names before the students get on the bus.","h":"قبل الصعود."},{"n":21,"s":"Where will the students go first in Taif?","o":["Al-Rudaf Park","Al-Shafa rose farms","the cable car at Al-Hada","a restaurant"],"k":1,"e":"[sequence] First, we will visit Al-Shafa rose farms.","h":"المكان الأول."},{"n":22,"s":"What will the students do after lunch?","o":["visit the rose farms","return the form","ride the cable car","check names"],"k":2,"e":"[sequence] After lunch, students will ride the cable car at Al-Hada.","h":"بعد الغداء."},{"n":23,"s":"Which item is NOT on the packing list?","o":["a jacket","a camera","sunscreen","a water bottle"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] jacket, water bottle, sunscreen, snack — no camera.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":24,"s":"What is the main purpose of this letter?","o":["to ask parents to drive to Taif","to give parents the plan for a school trip","to describe a rose farm","to sell cable car tickets"],"k":1,"e":"[purpose] It explains the plan and steps for the trip.","h":"خطة الرحلة."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 25–30): How bees make honey","(142 words)","Honey is made by bees in a long and careful process. First, worker bees fly from flower to flower and collect a sweet liquid called nectar. They store it in a special stomach, which is different from the stomach they use for food.","When a bee returns to the hive, it passes the nectar to another bee by mouth. This bee chews the nectar for about half an hour and then puts it into a small wax cell. At this stage, the nectar is still very watery.","Next, the bees fan the cells with their wings. This dries the nectar and turns it into thick honey. Finally, when the honey is ready, the bees cover each cell with a thin layer of wax to keep it clean. One bee makes only about one-twelfth of a teaspoon of honey in its whole life."],"q":[{"n":25,"s":"What do worker bees do first?","o":["fan the cells with their wings","cover the cells with wax","chew the nectar","collect nectar from flowers"],"k":3,"e":"[sequence] First, worker bees fly from flower to flower and collect … nectar.","h":"الخطوة الأولى."},{"n":26,"s":"Where do bees store nectar while flying?","o":["in a wax cell","on their wings","in a special stomach","in a flower"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] They store it in a special stomach.","h":"معدة خاصة."},{"n":27,"s":"What happens after a bee returns to the hive?","o":["It passes the nectar to another bee.","It flies to more flowers.","It covers the cell with wax.","It eats the honey."],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] When a bee returns to the hive, it passes the nectar to another bee.","h":"بعد العودة."},{"n":28,"s":"Why do bees fan the cells with their wings?","o":["to keep the hive cool for people","to find new flowers","to dry the nectar","to clean the wax"],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] This dries the nectar and turns it into thick honey.","h":"لتجفيف الرحيق."},{"n":29,"s":"What is the last step in the process?","o":["chewing the nectar","fanning the cells","collecting nectar","covering the cells with wax"],"k":3,"e":"[sequence] Finally … cover each cell with a thin layer of wax.","h":"الخطوة الأخيرة."},{"n":30,"s":"The word watery is closest in meaning to …","o":["thick and sticky","very sweet","thin, with a lot of water","hard"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] still very watery … then dried into thick honey.","h":"مائي / رقيق."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.5","t":"Cause and Effect","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.5 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify causes and effects signalled by because, so and as a result.</p>\n<p>2. Answer why questions with evidence from the text.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب السبب والنتيجة من خلال because وso وas a result.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يجيب عن أسئلة لماذا بدليل من النص.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A cause is WHY something happens; an effect is WHAT happens. Writers show this with signal words: because, since, as, because of, due to (cause) and so, as a result, therefore, that is why (effect).</p>\n<p>STEP asks: Why did …? What was the result of …? What caused …? The answer must be supported by the text, not by your general knowledge.</p>\n<p>Sometimes there is no signal word, and you must connect two sentences: The pipe broke. Water covered the floor. (cause → effect).</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ Why did …?</p>\n<p>▸ What was the result of …?</p>\n<p>▸ What caused …?</p>\n<p>▸ According to the text, … because …</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السبب هو لماذا يحدث الشيء، والنتيجة هي ما يحدث. وتدل على السبب كلمات مثل because وsince وdue to، وعلى النتيجة كلمات مثل so وas a result وtherefore. ويجب أن تكون الإجابة من النص لا من معلوماتك العامة.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Decide if the question asks for a cause (Why …?) or an effect (What happened as a result …?).</p>\n<p>2. Find the event from the question in the text.</p>\n<p>3. Look for a signal word next to it: because, so, as a result, due to.</p>\n<p>4. If there is no signal word, read the sentence before and after.</p>\n<p>5. Check that the option matches the text exactly — not just a possible reason from real life.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدد هل يسأل السؤال عن السبب أم النتيجة، ثم ابحث عن الحدث في النص وعن كلمة الربط بجانبه. وإن لم توجد فاقرأ الجملة السابقة واللاحقة، وتأكد أن الإجابة مذكورة في النص لا مجرد سبب منطقي من الواقع.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Choosing the effect when the question asks for the cause (and the opposite).</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing a reason that is logical in real life but not in the text.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing a cause of a different event in the same text.</p>\n<p>✗ Mixing up because (cause) and so (effect).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: The Power Cut</strong></p>\n<p><em>(45 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Last night, there was a storm, and strong winds damaged a power line near our street. As a result, all the houses lost electricity for three hours. Because the fridge was off, my mother put the milk and meat in a cool box with ice.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. What caused the power cut?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. The fridge was off.</p>\n<p>B. Strong winds damaged a power line.</p>\n<p>C. The houses used too much electricity.</p>\n<p>D. The mother used a cool box.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Question asks for a cause.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Strong winds damaged a power line. As a result, the houses lost electricity.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Why did the mother use a cool box?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. The fridge was off. B. She was going on a trip.</p>\n<p>C. The milk was too hot. D. The meat was frozen.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Signal word: because.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Because the fridge was off, my mother put the milk and meat in a cool box.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">as a result تأتي قبل النتيجة، وbecause تأتي قبل السبب.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 A","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–6): Why a student missed the bus","(128 words)","Last Monday, Khalid missed the school bus for the first time this year. The night before, he played video games until midnight, so he was very tired in the morning. He did not hear his alarm clock, and his mother had to wake him up at 6:40.","He dressed quickly, but he could not find his school bag because he had left it in the living room. By the time he found it, the bus had already left. As a result, his father had to drive him to school, and he was late for an important meeting at work.","Khalid felt bad. Since that day, he has put his phone away at ten o'clock and prepared his bag every evening. He has not missed the bus again."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Why was Khalid very tired in the morning?","o":["He walked to school.","He played video games until midnight.","He had a meeting at work.","He looked for his bag all night."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] played video games until midnight, so he was very tired.","h":"السهر."},{"n":2,"s":"Why could Khalid not find his bag?","o":["His brother had taken it.","It was on the bus.","His mother had hidden it.","He had left it in the living room."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] because he had left it in the living room.","h":"تركها في الصالة."},{"n":3,"s":"What was the result of Khalid missing the bus?","o":["Khalid missed an exam.","His father was late for a meeting.","The bus came back for him.","His mother drove the bus."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] As a result, his father had to drive him … and he was late for an important meeting.","h":"النتيجة."},{"n":4,"s":"What time did his mother wake him up?","o":["midnight","10:00","6:40","6:00"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] his mother had to wake him up at 6:40.","h":"6:40."},{"n":5,"s":"What has Khalid done since that day?","o":["He puts his phone away at ten and prepares his bag.","He sleeps at school.","He buys a new alarm clock every week.","He walks to school every day."],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Since that day, he has put his phone away at ten o'clock and prepared his bag.","h":"تغيير عاداته."},{"n":6,"s":"Why did Khalid feel bad?","o":["He lost his video games.","His teacher shouted at him.","His mistake caused problems for his father.","He was ill."],"k":2,"e":"[inference] His father was late for work because of him.","h":"شعر بالذنب."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 7–12): Too much screen time and tired eyes","(124 words)","Many young people spend more than six hours a day looking at screens: phones, tablets, computers and televisions. Doctors say this can cause a problem called digital eye strain. Because we blink less when we look at a screen, our eyes become dry and tired. Some people also get headaches or blurry vision.","Screen light can affect sleep too. Phones and tablets give out blue light, which tells the brain that it is still daytime. As a result, people who use screens in bed often find it hard to fall asleep.","Eye doctors suggest a simple rule called 20-20-20: every twenty minutes, look at something twenty feet (about six metres) away for twenty seconds. They also advise turning off screens one hour before bedtime."],"q":[{"n":7,"s":"According to the text, why do our eyes become dry when we look at screens?","o":["The room is too hot.","We blink less.","Screens are too small.","We sleep too much."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] Because we blink less when we look at a screen, our eyes become dry.","h":"نرمش أقل."},{"n":8,"s":"What does blue light tell the brain?","o":["that it is time to sleep","that the eyes are dry","that it is still daytime","that the screen is off"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] blue light, which tells the brain that it is still daytime.","h":"أنه نهار."},{"n":9,"s":"What is a result of using screens in bed?","o":["better vision","fewer headaches","waking up early","finding it hard to fall asleep"],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] As a result, people who use screens in bed often find it hard to fall asleep.","h":"صعوبة النوم."},{"n":10,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as an effect of too much screen time?","o":["headaches","earache","dry eyes","blurry vision"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] headaches ✓ dry eyes ✓ blurry vision ✓; earache ✗.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":11,"s":"In the 20-20-20 rule, how long should you look at something far away?","o":["twenty minutes","twenty seconds","six minutes","one hour"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] for twenty seconds.","h":"عشرون ثانية."},{"n":12,"s":"The word blurry is closest in meaning to …","o":["very bright","very dark","not clear","red"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] headaches or blurry vision → eyes can't see clearly.","h":"غير واضح."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 13–18): Why the roads are busy on Thursday evenings","(128 words)","Anyone who drives in Riyadh knows that the roads are very busy on Thursday evenings. There are several reasons for this. First, Thursday is the last working day of the week, so many people leave work at the same time and go straight out.","Second, families like to visit relatives, eat at restaurants or go shopping at the start of the weekend. Many weddings also take place on Thursday nights, and guests travel across the city to wedding halls.","Because of all this traffic, a journey that usually takes twenty minutes can take more than an hour. As a result, some people prefer to go out on Friday afternoon instead. The city is also building new metro lines, and experts hope these will reduce traffic in the future."],"q":[{"n":13,"s":"Why do many people go out at the same time on Thursday?","o":["Shops are closed on Friday.","It is the last working day of the week.","The metro is free on Thursday.","Schools open late on Thursday."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] Thursday is the last working day of the week, so many people leave work at the same time.","h":"آخر يوم عمل."},{"n":14,"s":"Why do wedding guests add to the traffic?","o":["They drive very slowly.","They park on the roads.","They travel across the city to wedding halls.","They go shopping first."],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] guests travel across the city to wedding halls.","h":"التنقل للأعراس."},{"n":15,"s":"What is the result of the heavy traffic?","o":["People stay at work longer.","Restaurants close early.","Weddings move to Friday.","A short journey can take more than an hour."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] a journey that usually takes twenty minutes can take more than an hour.","h":"رحلة أطول."},{"n":16,"s":"What do some people do because of the traffic?","o":["stay at work on Thursday","walk to restaurants","cancel weddings","go out on Friday afternoon instead"],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] As a result, some people prefer to go out on Friday afternoon.","h":"الخروج يوم الجمعة."},{"n":17,"s":"What do experts hope the new metro lines will do?","o":["reduce traffic","build more wedding halls","make journeys longer","open more restaurants"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] experts hope these will reduce traffic.","h":"تقليل الزحام."},{"n":18,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["how to plan a wedding","the history of Riyadh's metro","the best restaurants in Riyadh","the reasons for busy roads on Thursday evenings"],"k":3,"e":"[main idea] The text explains why the roads are busy.","h":"أسباب الزحام."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 19–24): A broken water pipe at school","(139 words)","On Sunday morning, a water pipe broke under the floor of the boys' toilets at Al-Rashid Primary School. Water came up through the floor and flowed into the corridor. Because the corridor is next to the library, the caretaker quickly moved the books on the lowest shelves to a higher place.","The head teacher turned off the main water supply, so there was no water in the whole school. As a result, students could not drink from the fountains or wash their hands. The school sent text messages to parents, and most students went home at ten o'clock.","A plumber came at eleven and repaired the pipe in three hours. He said the pipe was more than twenty years old and had become weak. The school has now decided to check all its old pipes during the summer holiday."],"q":[{"n":19,"s":"Why did the caretaker move the library books?","o":["The library was being painted.","The books were very old.","The water was flowing into the corridor next to the library.","The head teacher wanted new shelves."],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] Because the corridor is next to the library, the caretaker moved the books.","h":"قرب الماء من المكتبة."},{"n":20,"s":"What was the result of turning off the main water supply?","o":["There was no water in the whole school.","The pipe was repaired.","The library was closed for a week.","The students drank from the fountains."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] turned off the main water supply, so there was no water in the whole school.","h":"انقطاع الماء."},{"n":21,"s":"Why did most students go home at ten o'clock?","o":["The plumber asked them to.","There was no water at school.","It was a holiday.","The library was flooded."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] Students could not drink or wash their hands, so the school sent them home.","h":"بسبب انقطاع الماء."},{"n":22,"s":"How long did the plumber take to repair the pipe?","o":["three hours","eleven hours","twenty minutes","one day"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] repaired the pipe in three hours.","h":"ثلاث ساعات."},{"n":23,"s":"According to the plumber, why did the pipe break?","o":["It was old and had become weak.","Students damaged it.","It was too small.","The water was too hot."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] more than twenty years old and had become weak.","h":"قديم وضعيف."},{"n":24,"s":"What has the school decided to do?","o":["build a new library","close the boys' toilets","check all its old pipes in the summer","buy water fountains"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] check all its old pipes during the summer holiday.","h":"فحص الأنابيب."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 25–30): How exercise improves your mood","(126 words)","Most people know that exercise is good for the body, but it is also good for the mind. When you exercise, your brain releases chemicals called endorphins. These chemicals make you feel happier and more relaxed. That is why many people feel calm after a walk or a game of football.","Exercise also helps you sleep better. People who are active during the day usually fall asleep faster and wake up feeling fresh. Because they sleep well, they can concentrate more at school or at work.","You do not need to go to a gym. Experts say thirty minutes of walking, cycling or playing a sport on most days is enough. Exercising with friends is even better, because talking and laughing together also improves your mood."],"q":[{"n":25,"s":"What causes people to feel happier after exercise?","o":["a long sleep","talking to doctors","eating after sport","chemicals called endorphins"],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] your brain releases chemicals called endorphins. These chemicals make you feel happier.","h":"الإندورفين."},{"n":26,"s":"The phrase That is why in paragraph 1 introduces …","o":["a result","a cause","an example of a sport","a question"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] That is why = result of endorphins.","h":"نتيجة."},{"n":27,"s":"Why can active people concentrate more?","o":["They eat more.","They go to the gym.","They talk to friends at school.","They sleep well."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] Because they sleep well, they can concentrate more.","h":"النوم الجيد."},{"n":28,"s":"How much exercise do experts recommend?","o":["three hours every day","thirty minutes on most days","one hour a week","ten minutes on Fridays"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] thirty minutes … on most days is enough.","h":"ثلاثون دقيقة."},{"n":29,"s":"Why is exercising with friends even better?","o":["Talking and laughing also improve your mood.","Friends can pay for the gym.","It is faster.","Friends tell you what to eat."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] because talking and laughing together also improves your mood.","h":"الضحك والحديث."},{"n":30,"s":"The word mood is closest in meaning to …","o":["the way you feel","the way you walk","your weight","your school marks"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] improves your mood → feelings.","h":"المزاج."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.6","t":"Short Articles, Emails and Adverts","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.6 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify the writer's purpose in everyday texts.</p>\n<p>2. Find key information in adverts and emails.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب غرض الكاتب في النصوص اليومية.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يجد المعلومات الأساسية في الإعلانات والرسائل الإلكترونية.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Adverts try to persuade you to buy or join something. Emails may thank, ask, inform, complain or invite. Short articles usually inform or explain.</p>\n<p>STEP asks: Why did the writer write this email? What is the purpose of the advert? Who is the advert for? Look at the subject line, the first sentence and the last sentence.</p>\n<p>Adverts and emails also contain practical details: prices, dates, conditions (only for, must, if) and contact information. Read conditions carefully.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ What is the main purpose of the email?</p>\n<p>▸ Who is the advert for?</p>\n<p>▸ Why did … write to …?</p>\n<p>▸ Which of the following is a condition in the advert?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الإعلان يحاول إقناعك بالشراء أو الاشتراك، والرسالة قد تشكر أو تسأل أو تخبر أو تشتكي أو تدعو، والمقال القصير يخبر أو يشرح. ولمعرفة الغرض اقرأ سطر الموضوع والجملة الأولى والأخيرة، وانتبه للشروط مثل only for وmust وif.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Identify the text type: advert, email or article.</p>\n<p>2. Read the subject line or headline and the first sentence: they usually show the purpose.</p>\n<p>3. Find who the text is for (age, level, place).</p>\n<p>4. Underline numbers, dates, prices and conditions.</p>\n<p>5. For purpose questions, use verbs: to thank, to ask, to inform, to persuade, to complain.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدد نوع النص، واقرأ العنوان والجملة الأولى لمعرفة الغرض، وحدد لمن كُتب النص، وضع خطًا تحت الأرقام والتواريخ والأسعار والشروط، وصِف الغرض بفعل مثل to thank وto ask وto inform.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Choosing a detail instead of the purpose.</p>\n<p>✗ Confusing the writer with the reader of the email.</p>\n<p>✗ Missing a condition such as only, before, or must.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing to complain when the writer is only asking for information.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: Lost Cat</strong></p>\n<p><em>(47 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>LOST CAT — PLEASE HELP!</p>\n<p>Our grey cat, Smoky, has been missing since Sunday evening near Al-Wurud Park. She has a red collar with a small bell. She is friendly but may be frightened. If you see her, please call Nawaf on 054 321 8877. Reward: 200 riyals.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. What is the purpose of this notice?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. to sell a cat B. to ask people to help find a cat</p>\n<p>C. to advertise a park D. to give advice about pets</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Headline: LOST CAT — PLEASE HELP!</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The writer wants people to look for the cat.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. What should you do if you see Smoky?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. take her to the park B. call Nawaf</p>\n<p>C. buy her a collar D. pay 200 riyals</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Condition: If you see her, please call Nawaf.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العنوان والجملة الأولى يحددان الغرض، والشرط If you see her يحدد المطلوب.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 B","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–6): An advert for a summer English course","(128 words)","SUMMER ENGLISH CAMP 2026 — Learn, Speak, Enjoy!","Are you aged 12 to 16? Do you want to improve your English before the new school year? Join our four-week summer camp at Bright Future Language Centre, Al-Malqa, Riyadh.","Classes: Sunday to Thursday, 4:00 – 7:00 p.m. Small groups of no more than 10 students. All teachers are native speakers or have international teaching certificates.","Activities include drama, debates, a film club and a trip to a science museum. Every student receives a certificate at the end of the camp. Price: 2,400 riyals. Register before 15 June and get a 15% discount. Brothers and sisters get an extra 10% off.","Places are limited! Call 011 456 7788 or visit our website to book a free placement test."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What is the main purpose of the advert?","o":["to describe a science museum","to sell English books","to persuade students to join a summer course","to invite teachers to apply for jobs"],"k":2,"e":"[purpose] Join our four-week summer camp.","h":"الإقناع بالالتحاق."},{"n":2,"s":"Who is the camp for?","o":["children under 12","students aged 12 to 16","English teachers","parents"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Are you aged 12 to 16?","h":"من 12 إلى 16."},{"n":3,"s":"How many hours are the classes each day?","o":["four","seven","ten","three"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] 4:00 – 7:00 p.m. = 3 hours.","h":"ثلاث ساعات."},{"n":4,"s":"How can students get a 15% discount?","o":["by registering before 15 June","by bringing a brother or sister","by taking the placement test","by joining the film club"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Register before 15 June and get a 15% discount.","h":"التسجيل المبكر."},{"n":5,"s":"Which activity is NOT mentioned?","o":["a swimming competition","drama","debates","a film club"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] drama ✓ debates ✓ film club ✓; swimming ✗.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":6,"s":"The phrase Places are limited means …","o":["the camp is in many places","the centre is far away","only a small number of students can join","the course is free"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] limited places → not many seats.","h":"الأماكن محدودة."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 7–12): An email thanking a host family","(130 words)","Subject: Thank you for a wonderful month!","Dear Mr. and Mrs. Wilson,","I am writing to thank you for everything you did for me during my stay in Brighton. I arrived feeling nervous, but you made me feel like part of your family from the first day. Thank you especially for the delicious dinners, and for driving me to the station when I missed the bus in the rain!","My English has improved a lot. I now understand fast conversations much better, and I am not afraid to speak. Please say thank you to Emily for helping me with my homework and teaching me card games.","I hope you can visit Saudi Arabia one day. My parents would love to welcome you to our home in Jeddah.","Best wishes,","Osama"],"q":[{"n":7,"s":"What is the main purpose of Osama's email?","o":["to thank his host family","to complain about the weather","to ask for help with homework","to book a room in Brighton"],"k":0,"e":"[purpose] Subject: Thank you … I am writing to thank you.","h":"الشكر."},{"n":8,"s":"How did Osama feel when he arrived?","o":["angry","bored","ill","nervous"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] I arrived feeling nervous.","h":"متوتر."},{"n":9,"s":"Why did the Wilsons drive Osama to the station?","o":["His train was late.","He was ill.","He had missed the bus in the rain.","He had lost his ticket."],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] driving me to the station when I missed the bus in the rain.","h":"فاتته الحافلة."},{"n":10,"s":"Who is Emily probably?","o":["Osama's English teacher in Jeddah","Osama's sister","a member of the Wilson family","a bus driver"],"k":2,"e":"[inference] Please say thank you to Emily — she lives with the family.","h":"من العائلة."},{"n":11,"s":"What does Osama say about his English?","o":["He still cannot speak.","He understands fast conversations better.","He forgot many words.","He only learned card games."],"k":1,"e":"[detail] I now understand fast conversations much better.","h":"تحسّن فهمه."},{"n":12,"s":"What does Osama invite the Wilsons to do?","o":["send him more homework","come to Brighton station","teach his parents English","visit his family in Jeddah"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] My parents would love to welcome you to our home in Jeddah.","h":"زيارة جدة."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 13–18): A short article about a new cycling track","(129 words)","New Cycling Track Opens in Abha","A new cycling track opened in Abha last week, and it is already very popular with families. The track is 12 kilometres long and goes around the lake in the centre of the city. It is separate from the road, so cyclists do not need to worry about cars.","There are rest areas every two kilometres with benches, shade and drinking water. Visitors who do not have bicycles can rent one at the main entrance for 20 riyals an hour. Children under 12 must wear a helmet and ride with an adult.","The city council says the track is part of a plan to encourage people to exercise more and use their cars less. Another track will open in Khamis Mushait next year."],"q":[{"n":13,"s":"What is the main purpose of the article?","o":["to sell bicycles","to inform readers about a new cycling track","to complain about cars","to explain how to ride a bicycle"],"k":1,"e":"[purpose] The article reports the opening and gives details.","h":"الإخبار."},{"n":14,"s":"How long is the track?","o":["12 kilometres","2 kilometres","20 kilometres","1 kilometre"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] The track is 12 kilometres long.","h":"12 كم."},{"n":15,"s":"Why do cyclists not need to worry about cars?","o":["Cars are not allowed in Abha.","The track is separate from the road.","There are police on the track.","The track is inside a building."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] It is separate from the road, so cyclists do not need to worry.","h":"منفصل عن الطريق."},{"n":16,"s":"What can you find every two kilometres?","o":["bicycle shops","car parks","restaurants","rest areas"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] There are rest areas every two kilometres.","h":"استراحات."},{"n":17,"s":"Which of the following is a rule for children under 12?","o":["They cannot rent bicycles.","They must wear a helmet and ride with an adult.","They must pay 20 riyals.","They can only ride in the morning."],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Children under 12 must wear a helmet and ride with an adult.","h":"شرط الأطفال."},{"n":18,"s":"Why did the council build the track?","o":["to encourage people to exercise and drive less","to make money from rentals","to clean the lake","to build a new road"],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] part of a plan to encourage people to exercise more and use their cars less.","h":"التشجيع على الرياضة."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 19–24): An advert for a second-hand bicycle","(132 words)","FOR SALE: Boy's mountain bike — excellent condition","I am selling my son's blue mountain bike because he has grown too tall for it. It is two years old but looks almost new. It has 21 gears, front and back brakes, and new tyres that I bought last month. The bike has always been kept inside, away from the sun and rain.","The bike is suitable for children aged 9 to 12 (height 130–150 cm). A helmet and a bike lock are included at no extra cost.","Price: 450 riyals (new price: 1,100 riyals). The price is fixed, so please do not ask for a discount.","You can see the bike in Al-Rawdah, Jeddah, any evening after 5 p.m. Please send a message first: 055 908 1122 (no calls, please)."],"q":[{"n":19,"s":"Why is the writer selling the bike?","o":["It is broken.","His son is now too tall for it.","He wants a bigger bike himself.","It is too old."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] because he has grown too tall for it.","h":"كبر الابن."},{"n":20,"s":"Who is the bike suitable for?","o":["adults","children under 5","children aged 9 to 12","teenagers aged 13 to 18"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] suitable for children aged 9 to 12.","h":"من 9 إلى 12."},{"n":21,"s":"What is included at no extra cost?","o":["a helmet and a lock","new tyres and gears","a second bike","delivery to your home"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] A helmet and a bike lock are included at no extra cost.","h":"خوذة وقفل."},{"n":22,"s":"What does The price is fixed mean?","o":["The bike has been repaired.","The price is very cheap.","You can pay later.","The price will not change."],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] fixed → do not ask for a discount.","h":"السعر ثابت."},{"n":23,"s":"How should buyers contact the seller?","o":["by calling at any time","by email","by sending a message","by visiting before 5 p.m."],"k":2,"e":"[detail] Please send a message first … (no calls, please).","h":"رسالة نصية."},{"n":24,"s":"How much cheaper is the bike than a new one?","o":["450 riyals","1,100 riyals","550 riyals","650 riyals"],"k":3,"e":"[inference] 1,100 − 450 = 650.","h":"الفرق 650."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 25–30): An email to a hotel asking about a room","(135 words)","Subject: Room enquiry for 18–21 March","Dear Sir or Madam,","I am planning a short holiday in Madinah with my wife and our two children, aged 6 and 9, from 18 to 21 March. I would like to ask a few questions before I make a booking.","First, do you have a family room with two large beds or one large bed and two small ones? Second, is breakfast included in the price? Third, how far is the hotel from the Prophet's Mosque, and do you offer a free bus?","We will arrive by train at about 10 p.m. on the 18th. Could you tell me if late check-in is possible? Finally, could you please send me the price for three nights?","I look forward to hearing from you.","Yours faithfully,","Majid Al-Dosari"],"q":[{"n":25,"s":"What is the main purpose of the email?","o":["to ask for information before booking","to complain about a room","to cancel a booking","to thank the hotel for a stay"],"k":0,"e":"[purpose] I would like to ask a few questions before I make a booking.","h":"الاستفسار."},{"n":26,"s":"How many people will stay at the hotel?","o":["two","three","four","six"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] my wife and our two children + Majid = 4.","h":"أربعة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which question does Majid NOT ask?","o":["whether breakfast is included","whether late check-in is possible","how far the hotel is from the mosque","whether the hotel has a swimming pool"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] No question about a pool.","h":"سؤال غير مطروح."},{"n":28,"s":"Why does Majid ask about late check-in?","o":["The children are young.","The family will arrive at about 10 p.m.","The hotel is far from the station.","He wants a free bus."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] We will arrive by train at about 10 p.m.","h":"الوصول متأخرًا."},{"n":29,"s":"How many nights will the family stay?","o":["four","two","three","eighteen"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] send me the price for three nights.","h":"ثلاث ليالٍ."},{"n":30,"s":"How will the family travel to Madinah?","o":["by plane","by car","by bus","by train"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] We will arrive by train.","h":"بالقطار."}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions on new texts. Read each text and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا على نصوص جديدة، اقرأ كل نص واختر الإجابة الصحيحة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–6): The longest river in the world","(137 words)","The Nile is often called the longest river in the world. It is about 6,650 kilometres long and flows through eleven countries in north-east Africa before it reaches the Mediterranean Sea in Egypt. However, some scientists believe that the Amazon in South America is slightly longer, so the question is still debated.","For thousands of years, the Nile has been essential for life in Egypt and Sudan. Most of the land around it is dry desert, but the river brings water for farms and drinking. Every summer in the past, the river flooded and left rich black soil on the fields. Because of this soil, farmers could grow wheat and vegetables easily.","In 1970, Egypt finished building the Aswan High Dam. Since then, the floods have stopped, and the dam produces electricity for millions of homes."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["The Nile: A River That Gives Life","Deserts of North-East Africa","How to Build a Dam","The Amazon in South America"],"k":0,"e":"[best title · 2.1] The text is about the Nile and its importance.","h":"النيل نهر الحياة."},{"n":2,"s":"How many countries does the Nile flow through?","o":["six","eleven","two","seventy"],"k":1,"e":"[detail · 2.2] flows through eleven countries.","h":"إحدى عشرة دولة."},{"n":3,"s":"The word essential is closest in meaning to …","o":["very dangerous","very old","very wide","very necessary"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] brings water for farms and drinking → necessary for life.","h":"ضروري."},{"n":4,"s":"Why could farmers grow wheat easily in the past?","o":["The dam gave them electricity.","It rained every day.","The river was very short.","The floods left rich black soil."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] Because of this soil, farmers could grow wheat.","h":"التربة الخصبة."},{"n":5,"s":"What happened after Egypt built the Aswan High Dam?","o":["The river became longer.","The floods stopped.","Farmers moved to Sudan.","The soil became black."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] Since then, the floods have stopped.","h":"بعد بناء السد."},{"n":6,"s":"Why is the question of the longest river still debated?","o":["Nobody has measured the Nile.","The Nile is getting shorter.","Egypt built a dam on it.","Some scientists think the Amazon is longer."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] some scientists believe the Amazon is slightly longer, so the question is still debated.","h":"الخلاف حول الأمازون."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 7–12): A school recycling competition","(142 words)","Last term, our school held a recycling competition between classes. The rules were simple: each class had to collect plastic bottles, cans and paper for six weeks. Every Thursday, the science teacher weighed the bags, and the results were written on a board in the main corridor.","At first, most classes collected only a few kilograms. Then Class 8C had a clever idea. They asked their families and neighbours to save recycling for them, and they put boxes in two local mosques and a supermarket. As a result, their total increased quickly.","At the end of the six weeks, Class 8C had collected 340 kilograms, more than twice as much as any other class. Their prize was a trip to a recycling factory in Dammam. The school sold all the materials and used the money to buy new benches for the playground."],"q":[{"n":7,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a recycling competition and how one class won it","the history of recycling factories","how to weigh plastic bottles","new benches in the playground"],"k":0,"e":"[main idea · 2.1] The text describes the competition and 8C's win.","h":"عن المسابقة."},{"n":8,"s":"Which of the following was NOT collected in the competition?","o":["plastic bottles","cans","glass jars","paper"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 2.2] bottles ✓ cans ✓ paper ✓; glass ✗.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":9,"s":"What happened every Thursday?","o":["Class 8C visited a factory.","Families brought boxes to school.","The science teacher weighed the bags.","The school bought benches."],"k":2,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] Every Thursday, the science teacher weighed the bags.","h":"كل خميس."},{"n":10,"s":"Why did Class 8C's total increase quickly?","o":["Families, neighbours and local places saved recycling for them.","They bought plastic bottles.","The teacher helped them.","The competition lasted longer for them."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] They asked their families … and put boxes … As a result, their total increased.","h":"سبب الزيادة."},{"n":11,"s":"The word increased is the opposite of …","o":["collected","weighed","won","decreased"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] increased (went up) ↔︎ decreased (went down).","h":"عكس increased."},{"n":12,"s":"What did the school do with the money?","o":["paid for the trip to Dammam","built a recycling factory","bought new benches for the playground","gave it to Class 8C"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 2.2] used the money to buy new benches for the playground.","h":"مقاعد جديدة."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 13–18): Learning Chinese at school","(127 words)","Subject: Chinese lessons for Grade 7","Dear Parents,","We are pleased to announce that, from next semester, all Grade 7 students will study Chinese for two lessons a week. Saudi Arabia and China have strong trade and cultural links, and many companies now need people who can speak Chinese. Learning a new language also improves memory and problem-solving.","The lessons will focus on speaking and listening at first. Students will learn greetings, numbers and simple conversations before they start reading Chinese characters. Our new teacher, Ms. Li Na, has taught Arabic speakers for eight years.","There will be an information evening on 3 May at 7 p.m. in the school hall. Please come and meet Ms. Li Na and ask any questions.","Mr. Abdulaziz, Head Teacher"],"q":[{"n":13,"s":"What is the main purpose of the email?","o":["to ask parents to teach Chinese","to inform parents about new Chinese lessons","to sell Chinese books","to complain about Grade 7"],"k":1,"e":"[purpose · 2.6] We are pleased to announce … Chinese lessons.","h":"الإعلان عن الدروس."},{"n":14,"s":"How many Chinese lessons a week will Grade 7 students have?","o":["three","seven","eight","two"],"k":3,"e":"[detail · 2.2] two lessons a week.","h":"درسان."},{"n":15,"s":"Why do many companies need Chinese speakers?","o":["Chinese is easy to learn.","Ms. Li Na works for a company.","Students asked for it.","Saudi Arabia and China have strong trade links."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] strong trade and cultural links, and many companies now need people who can speak Chinese.","h":"الروابط التجارية."},{"n":16,"s":"What will students learn before reading Chinese characters?","o":["Chinese history","greetings, numbers and simple conversations","how to write long essays","Arabic grammar"],"k":1,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] Students will learn greetings, numbers and simple conversations before they start reading.","h":"قبل القراءة."},{"n":17,"s":"Why should parents come on 3 May?","o":["to take a Chinese test","to watch a film","to meet the new teacher and ask questions","to pay for the lessons"],"k":2,"e":"[purpose · 2.6] Please come and meet Ms. Li Na and ask any questions.","h":"لقاء المعلمة."},{"n":18,"s":"The word announce is closest in meaning to …","o":["keep secret","ask a question","tell people officially","say sorry"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] We are pleased to announce → officially tell.","h":"يعلن."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 19–24): A volunteer at a food bank","(135 words)","Every Saturday morning, Huda, a 17-year-old student from Dammam, volunteers at a food bank. A food bank collects food from supermarkets, restaurants and families and gives it to people who need help.","Huda's day starts at eight o'clock. First, she and the other volunteers check the food that arrived during the week. They throw away anything that is damaged or past its date. Next, they sort the good food into groups: rice and flour, tins, oil, and dried fruit. After that, they pack boxes for families. Each box contains enough food for a family of five for one week.","At noon, the boxes are delivered to the families' homes. Huda says volunteering has made her more grateful for what she has. She also enjoys working in a team, and she has made good friends there."],"q":[{"n":19,"s":"What is the main idea of the text?","o":["A student helps families in need by volunteering at a food bank.","Supermarkets throw away a lot of food.","Dried fruit is healthy.","Students should work on Saturdays."],"k":0,"e":"[main idea · 2.1] The text describes Huda's volunteering.","h":"الفكرة الرئيسة."},{"n":20,"s":"What do the volunteers do first?","o":["pack boxes","deliver the boxes","check the food that arrived","sort the food into groups"],"k":2,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] First, she and the other volunteers check the food.","h":"الخطوة الأولى."},{"n":21,"s":"What happens to damaged food?","o":["It is given to restaurants.","It is sold.","It is packed in boxes.","It is thrown away."],"k":3,"e":"[detail · 2.2] They throw away anything that is damaged.","h":"يُرمى."},{"n":22,"s":"What happens at noon?","o":["The volunteers check the food.","Huda arrives.","The food is sorted.","The boxes are delivered."],"k":3,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] At noon, the boxes are delivered.","h":"عند الظهر."},{"n":23,"s":"The word grateful is closest in meaning to …","o":["thankful","worried","proud of herself","tired"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] more grateful for what she has → thankful.","h":"ممتن."},{"n":24,"s":"How much food does each box contain?","o":["enough for one person for a month","five kilograms of rice","enough for a family of five for one week","food for one day only"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 2.2] Each box contains enough food for a family of five for one week.","h":"محتوى الصندوق."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 25–30): How Saudi coffee is served to guests","(139 words)","In Saudi Arabia, serving coffee to guests is an important tradition and a sign of generosity. Saudi coffee is very different from the coffee in most cafés. It is made from lightly roasted beans and flavoured with cardamom, and sometimes with saffron or cloves. It is yellow-brown rather than black.","The coffee is poured from a special pot called a dallah into small cups without handles. The host holds the dallah in the left hand and the cups in the right. The oldest or most important guest is served first, and the cup is filled only a quarter full, so the coffee stays hot.","Guests usually drink one to three cups. When a guest has had enough, he gently shakes the cup from side to side. Coffee is almost always served with dates, which balance its bitter taste."],"q":[{"n":25,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["Coffee Shops Around the World","How to Grow Dates","The History of Saffron","How Saudi Coffee Is Served to Guests"],"k":3,"e":"[best title · 2.1] The text explains the tradition of serving Saudi coffee.","h":"العنوان الأفضل."},{"n":26,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a flavour in Saudi coffee?","o":["cardamom","cinnamon","saffron","cloves"],"k":1,"e":"[detail · 2.2] cardamom ✓ saffron ✓ cloves ✓; cinnamon ✗.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":27,"s":"Why is the cup filled only a quarter full?","o":["because the coffee is expensive","because guests do not like coffee","so the coffee stays hot","so the cup does not break"],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] filled only a quarter full, so the coffee stays hot.","h":"لتبقى ساخنة."},{"n":28,"s":"What does a guest do when he has had enough?","o":["puts the cup upside down","asks for dates","shakes the cup gently","gives the cup to the oldest guest"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 2.2] he gently shakes the cup from side to side.","h":"يهز الفنجان."},{"n":29,"s":"The word bitter is the opposite of …","o":["hot","sweet","yellow","strong"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] dates balance its bitter taste → dates are sweet.","h":"عكس bitter."},{"n":30,"s":"Who is served coffee first?","o":["the oldest or most important guest","the youngest guest","the host","the guest who arrives last"],"k":0,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] The oldest or most important guest is served first.","h":"من يُقدَّم له أولًا."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 31–35): A pilot's working day","(143 words)","Captain Saud Al-Harthi is a pilot for a Saudi airline. His working day starts long before passengers get on the plane. He arrives at the airport two hours before the flight and checks the weather, the route and the amount of fuel needed.","Next, he meets the co-pilot and the cabin crew to discuss the flight. Then he walks around the outside of the plane to check that everything looks correct. About forty minutes before take-off, the passengers start boarding. When everyone is seated and the doors are closed, the plane moves to the runway.","During a long flight, the two pilots take turns to rest. After landing, Captain Saud writes a short report about the flight. He says the job is tiring because of the long hours and changing time zones, but he still feels excited every time the plane takes off."],"q":[{"n":31,"s":"What does Captain Saud do as soon as he arrives at the airport?","o":["checks the weather, the route and the fuel","walks around the plane","meets the passengers","writes a report"],"k":0,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] He arrives … and checks the weather, the route and the amount of fuel.","h":"أول عمل."},{"n":32,"s":"What happens just before the plane moves to the runway?","o":["The pilots take turns to rest.","The passengers sit down and the doors are closed.","The captain writes a report.","The captain checks the fuel."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] When everyone is seated and the doors are closed, the plane moves to the runway.","h":"قبل التحرك."},{"n":33,"s":"Why is the job tiring?","o":["the passengers are noisy","the planes are old","long hours and changing time zones","the reports are long"],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] tiring because of the long hours and changing time zones.","h":"سبب التعب."},{"n":34,"s":"The phrase take turns means …","o":["do something at the same time","do something one after the other","stop working","turn the plane around"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] the two pilots take turns to rest → one rests, then the other.","h":"يتناوبان."},{"n":35,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a pilot's working day","how to become a pilot","airport shops","a passenger's journey"],"k":0,"e":"[main idea · 2.1] The text describes Captain Saud's day.","h":"يوم الطيار."}]},{"l":["Text 7 (Questions 36–40): The falcon in Arabian culture","(131 words)","Falcons have been part of Arabian culture for thousands of years. In the past, Bedouins trained falcons to hunt birds and small animals in the desert. This helped them find food when there was very little to eat.","Today, falconry is a popular sport and a symbol of courage and honour. Training a falcon takes a lot of time and patience. The falconer must feed the bird by hand, speak to it calmly and teach it to return when it is called. A well-trained falcon can fly at more than 300 kilometres an hour when it dives.","Every year, the King Abdulaziz Falcon Festival takes place near Riyadh. Falconers from many countries compete in speed and beauty competitions. In 2016, UNESCO added falconry to its list of important world heritage traditions."],"q":[{"n":36,"s":"Why did Bedouins train falcons in the past?","o":["to win competitions","to carry messages","to protect their tents","to help them find food"],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] trained falcons to hunt … This helped them find food.","h":"للحصول على الطعام."},{"n":37,"s":"The word courage is closest in meaning to …","o":["speed","bravery","beauty","patience"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] a symbol of courage and honour → bravery.","h":"الشجاعة."},{"n":38,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as part of training a falcon?","o":["feeding it by hand","speaking to it calmly","giving it medicine every day","teaching it to return"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 2.2] feeding ✓ speaking ✓ return ✓; medicine ✗.","h":"غير مذكور."},{"n":39,"s":"What happened in 2016?","o":["UNESCO added falconry to its list of world heritage traditions.","The first falcon festival took place.","Falcons flew at 300 km/h for the first time.","Bedouins stopped hunting."],"k":0,"e":"[detail · 2.2] In 2016, UNESCO added falconry to its list.","h":"عام 2016."},{"n":40,"s":"Which is the best title for the text?","o":["How Fast Birds Can Fly","Bedouin Tents","A Festival in Riyadh","The Falcon in Arabian Culture"],"k":3,"e":"[best title · 2.1] The text covers falcons in the past and today.","h":"العنوان الشامل."}]},{"l":["Text 8 (Questions 41–45): A school trip to the Edge of the World","(133 words)","Dear Parents,","On Thursday, Grade 9 will visit Jebel Fihrayn, which is known as the Edge of the World, about 90 kilometres north-west of Riyadh. From the top of the cliffs, students will see a huge, flat plain hundreds of metres below.","The buses will leave school at 5:30 a.m., because it is best to arrive before the day gets hot. When we arrive, a trained guide will lead a 45-minute walk to the viewpoint. Students must stay on the marked path and keep at least two metres from the edge.","Please make sure your child wears strong shoes and brings two litres of water, a hat and sunscreen. Phones may be used for photos, but no drones are allowed. We will return by 2 p.m.","Ms. Nouf, Trip Leader"],"q":[{"n":41,"s":"What is the main purpose of this letter?","o":["to give parents information about a school trip","to advertise a guided tour company","to ask parents to join the walk","to describe the history of Riyadh"],"k":0,"e":"[purpose · 2.6] It explains the plan, rules and what to bring.","h":"معلومات الرحلة."},{"n":42,"s":"Why will the buses leave so early?","o":["because the road is closed later","because the guide starts work early","to see the sunrise from the bus","to arrive before the day gets hot"],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] because it is best to arrive before the day gets hot.","h":"قبل الحر."},{"n":43,"s":"What will happen when the group arrives?","o":["Students will fly drones.","A guide will lead a walk to the viewpoint.","The group will have lunch.","The buses will return to school."],"k":1,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] When we arrive, a trained guide will lead a 45-minute walk.","h":"عند الوصول."},{"n":44,"s":"Which of the following is a rule in the letter?","o":["Students must bring a drone.","Phones are not allowed.","Students must keep at least two metres from the edge.","Students must walk alone."],"k":2,"e":"[purpose · 2.6] keep at least two metres from the edge.","h":"قاعدة."},{"n":45,"s":"The word huge is closest in meaning to …","o":["very large","very dry","very dangerous","very high"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] a huge, flat plain → very large.","h":"ضخم."}]},{"l":["Text 9 (Questions 46–50): Keeping a diary in English","(148 words)","My English teacher gave me an idea last year: keep a diary in English. At first, I thought it would be boring and difficult. However, I decided to try it for one month.","Every night before bed, I wrote five or six sentences about my day: what I did, what I ate and how I felt. When I did not know a word, I wrote it in Arabic and looked it up the next morning. After two weeks, I noticed that I was writing faster and using fewer Arabic words.","Now, a year later, I still write every night, and my diary is three notebooks long. My grammar has improved because I practise the past tense every day, and my teacher says my writing is much clearer. I also enjoy reading old pages and remembering funny moments. I recommend this habit to every student who wants to improve."],"q":[{"n":46,"s":"What did the writer think about keeping a diary at first?","o":["It would be fun and easy.","It would be boring and difficult.","It would take one year.","It would improve her grammar."],"k":1,"e":"[detail · 2.2] At first, I thought it would be boring and difficult.","h":"رأيها في البداية."},{"n":47,"s":"What did the writer do when she did not know a word?","o":["asked her teacher immediately","stopped writing","used a different word","wrote it in Arabic and looked it up the next morning"],"k":3,"e":"[sequence · 2.4] I wrote it in Arabic and looked it up the next morning.","h":"كتبتها بالعربية."},{"n":48,"s":"Why has the writer's grammar improved?","o":["She reads old pages.","She practises the past tense every day.","She has three notebooks.","Her teacher corrects her diary."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect · 2.5] My grammar has improved because I practise the past tense every day.","h":"ممارسة الماضي."},{"n":49,"s":"The word recommend is closest in meaning to …","o":["refuse","forget","suggest as a good idea","complain about"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 2.3] I recommend this habit to every student → suggest.","h":"يوصي."},{"n":50,"s":"What is the main purpose of the text?","o":["to encourage students to keep a diary in English","to sell notebooks","to complain about English teachers","to explain the past tense"],"k":0,"e":"[purpose · 2.6] I recommend this habit to every student who wants to improve.","h":"التشجيع."}]}],"n":50}};
